     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Details on the replacement are explained at <a href=\"https://github.com/jcfaria/Vim-R-plugin/issues/204\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jcfaria/Vim-R-plugin/issues/204&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494165475000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3E5qdV6rwIa4FiUrEvMB5X\">https://github.com/jcfaria/Vim-R-plugin/issues/204</a><div><br></div><div>On Windows, users have two options:</div><div><ul><li>Use the released versions of Nvim-R and nvimcom, both available at <a href=\"https://github.com/jalvesaq/Nvim-R/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jalvesaq/Nvim-R/releases&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494165475000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1n-CzGsVfqT-egXx-NYWWd\">Nvim-R/releases</a> (note that nvimcom is released only when needed and currently the last nvimcom binary (0.9-14) was released with Nvim-R 0.9.2).<br></li><li>Install the development version of Nvim-R and install <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/Rtools/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/Rtools/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494165475000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ogTCSBNEBd1hH9uhD6alu\">Rtools</a> to be able to build nvimcom yourself.<br></li></ul></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
